	"summary": {
		"text": "The Fakkawa are the people of Fakai in southern Kebbi State. Their speech, called Fakkanci in Hausa and Kag in Amfani's survey, is the Kainji language Glottolog lists as Ut-Ma'in (Kag-Fer-Jiir-Koor-Ror-Us-Zuksun, after its dialects). It is also spoken in Zuru and Sakaba, in Kebbe LGA of Sokoto, and in Anka LGA of Zamfara.",
